  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Circular South Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In South Africa, an adequate understanding of circularity is lacking with businesses and many other important stakeholders as it is often conceived as related to waste only. Circular economy however is an important instrument to tackle the current planetary crises on climate, biodiversity and pollution. By keeping resources in the loop for longer, the project partners will avoid emitting greenhouse gases caused by the energy needed to make products.This project serves to support South Africa in its transition to a circular economy by establishing a platform to facilitate cooperation, coordination and networking between businesses, government, knowledge institutions, civil society organisations and other relevant actors involved in the circular economy.It aspires to enable public/private partnerships, engage in a matchmaker role and facilitate the transition through, inter alia, engagement on policies, aligning finance, networking partners, facilitating a knowledge hub or one-stop-shop, &#x201c;accelerating&#x201d; the transition, fast-tracking implementation, identifying opportunities or project gaps, and general communications and advocacy across regions and sector focus areas.The platform will also have an agenda-setting role for a more coordinated and demand-driven approach toward a circular economy that drives local entrepreneurship, creates jobs and contributes to sustainable economic growth.The project is a follow-up of the study &#x2018;Exploring a South Africa Circular Economy Platform&#x2019; (PST21ZA01), conducted in 2022.</narrative>
  </description>
